\f1\b \cf2 1. Choose the correct collective noun to fill in the blank:
\f0\b0 \
\
A __________ of wolves was seen roaming through the snowy valley.\
\
(A) herd\
\
(B) pack\
\
(C) pride\
\
(D) swarm\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B) pack.
\f0\b0 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf2 Explanation:
\f0\i0  A group of wolves (or wild dogs/playing cards) is called a 
\f2\i pack
\f0\i0 . A 
\f2\i pride
\f0\i0  refers to lions, a 
\f2\i herd
\f0\i0  to cattle/elephants, and a 
\f2\i swarm
\f0\i0  to insects.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf2 2. Fill in the blank with the appropriate relative pronoun:
\f0\b0 \
\
The boy __________ won the first prize in the debate is my cousin.\
\
(A) which\
\
(B) whom\
\
(C) who\
\
(D) whose\
\

\f1\b Answer: (C) who.
\f0\b0 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf2 Explanation:
\f0\i0  Use 
\f2\i who
\f0\i0  as a subject pronoun referring to a person ("The boy won the prize").\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf2 3. Fill in the blank with the correct degree of adjective:
\f0\b0 \
\
Mount Everest is the __________ mountain peak in the world.\
\
(A) high\
\
(B) higher\
\
(C) highest\
\
(D) most high\
\

\f1\b Answer: (C) highest.
\f0\b0 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf2 Explanation:
\f0\i0  When comparing more than two entities or specifying an absolute peak with "the", the superlative degree (
\f2\i highest
\f0\i0 ) is used.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf2 4. Choose the appropriate article to complete the sentence:
\f0\b0 \
\
Rohan waited for almost __________ hour at the bus stop.\
\
(A) a\
\
(B) an\
\
(C) the\
\
(D) no article\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B) an.
\f0\b0 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf2 Explanation:
\f0\i0  The word "hour" begins with a silent 'h' and has a vowel sound (/a\uc0\u650 \u601 r/), so the indefinite article 
\f2\i an
\f0\i0  is used.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf2 5. Fill in the blank with the correct form of the verb:
\f0\b0 \
\
A bouquet of fresh roses __________ placed on the dining table yesterday.\
\
(A) were\
\
(B) was\
\
(C) are\
\
(D) have been\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B) was.
\f0\b0 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf2 Explanation:
\f0\i0  The subject is the singular collective noun "A bouquet" (not "roses"). Since the action took place "yesterday", the singular past verb 
\f2\i was
\f0\i0  is correct.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf2 6. Choose the correct tense to complete the sentence:
\f0\b0 \
\
Priya __________ her homework before her mother arrived from the market.\
\
(A) has finished\
\
(B) had finished\
\
(C) finishes\
\
(D) will finish\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B) had finished.
\f0\b0 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf2 Explanation:
\f0\i0  Past Perfect tense (
\f2\i had finished
\f0\i0 ) is used for an action completed before another past event ("arrived").\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf2 7. Choose the correct modal verb to express polite permission:
\f0\b0 \
\
"Excuse me, teacher. __________ I drink some water, please?"\
\
(A) Might\
\
(B) Must\
\
(C) May\
\
(D) Should\
\

\f1\b Answer: (C) May.
\f0\b0 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf2 Explanation:
\f0\i0  
\f2\i May
\f0\i0  is the standard, polite modal auxiliary used for asking formal permission.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf2 8. Fill in the blank with the correct preposition of time:
\f0\b0 \
\
The annual school concert will begin __________ 5:00 PM sharp.\
\
(A) on\
\
(B) in\
\
(C) at\
\
(D) by\
\

\f1\b Answer: (C) at.
\f0\b0 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf2 Explanation:
\f0\i0  We use the preposition 
\f2\i at
\f0\i0  for specific clock times (e.g., 
\f2\i at 5:00 PM
\f0\i0 , 
\f2\i at noon
\f0\i0 ).\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf2 9. Choose the appropriate conjunction to join the two clauses:
\f0\b0 \
\
Aman ran very fast, __________ he missed the morning school bus.\
\
(A) because\
\
(B) but\
\
(C) so\
\
(D) unless\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B) but.
\f0\b0 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf2 Explanation:
\f0\i0  
\f2\i But
\f0\i0  shows contrast between running fast and still missing the bus.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf2 10. Identify the adverb of manner in the given sentence:
\f0\b0 \
\
The little girl sang the prayer melodiously during the morning assembly.\
\
(A) little\
\
(B) morning\
\
(C) melodiously\
\
(D) during\
\

\f1\b Answer: (C) melodiously.
\f0\b0 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf2 Explanation:
\f0\i0  "Melodiously" answers 
\f2\i how
\f0\i0  the action was performed (adverb of manner).\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf2 11. Convert the following sentence into Passive Voice:
\f0\b0 \
\
"The chef prepared a delicious meal."\
\
(A) A delicious meal is prepared by the chef.\
\
(B) A delicious meal was prepared by the chef.\
\
(C) A delicious meal had prepared by the chef.\
\
(D) A delicious meal will be prepared by the chef.\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B) A delicious meal was prepared by the chef.
\f0\b0 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf2 Explanation:
\f0\i0  Simple Past active ("prepared") converts to 
\f2\i was/were + past participle
\f0\i0  ("was prepared").\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf2 12. Convert the direct speech into reported (indirect) speech:
\f0\b0 \
\
Kavita said, "I am reading an interesting storybook."\
\
(A) Kavita said that she is reading an interesting storybook.\
\
(B) Kavita said that she was reading an interesting storybook.\
\
(C) Kavita said that I was reading an interesting storybook.\
\
(D) Kavita said that she had read an interesting storybook.\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B) Kavita said that she was reading an interesting storybook.
\f0\b0 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf2 Explanation:
\f0\i0  Present Continuous ("am reading") shifts back into Past Continuous ("was reading"), and pronoun "I" changes to "she".\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf2 13. Choose the synonym of the underlined word:
\f0\b0 \
\
The king was known throughout the kingdom for being 
\f1\b generous
\f0\b0  to the poor.\
\
(A) greedy\
\
(B) charitable\
\
(C) cruel\
\
(D) timid\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B) charitable.
\f0\b0 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf2 Explanation:
\f0\i0  "Generous" means willing to give help or kindness freely; "charitable" is the closest synonym.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf2 14. Choose the antonym of the underlined word:
\f0\b0 \
\
The glass vase on the shelf is extremely 
\f1\b fragile
\f0\b0 .\
\
(A) delicate\
\
(B) brittle\
\
(C) sturdy\
\
(D) smooth\
\

\f1\b Answer: (C) sturdy.
\f0\b0 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf2 Explanation:
\f0\i0  "Fragile" means easily broken; its opposite is "sturdy" (strong and robust).\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf2 15. Choose the correct word to fill in the blank (Homophones):
\f0\b0 \
\
Please buy a packet of envelopes from the nearest __________ shop.\
\
(A) stationary\
\
(B) stationery\
\
(C) stationer\
\
(D) stationry\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B) stationery.
\f0\b0 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf2 Explanation:
\f0\i0  "Stationery" (with an 'e') refers to writing and office materials. "Stationary" (with an 'a') means unmoving.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf2 16. Select the correctly spelt word:
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Accomodation\
\
(B) Acommodation\
\
(C) Accommodation\
\
(D) Acomodation\
\

\f1\b Answer: (C) Accommodation.
\f0\b0 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf2 Explanation:
\f0\i0  It contains double 'c' and double 'm': A-c-c-o-m-m-o-d-a-t-i-o-n.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf2 17. Choose the correct prefix to form the opposite of the word "RESPONSIBLE":
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Un-\
\
(B) Dis-\
\
(C) Ir-\
\
(D) In-\
\

\f1\b Answer: (C) Ir-.
\f0\b0 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf2 Explanation:
\f0\i0  Words beginning with 'r' frequently take the prefix 
\f2\i ir-
\f0\i0  to form antonyms (e.g., 
\f2\i irresponsible
\f0\i0 , 
\f2\i irregular
\f0\i0 ).\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf2 18. Give one word for: "A person who writes books, articles, or stories."
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Sculptor\
\
(B) Architect\
\
(C) Author\
\
(D) Curator\
\

\f1\b Answer: (C) Author.
\f0\b0 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf2 Explanation:
\f0\i0  An author is a writer of books, poems, or articles.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf2 19. Fill in the blank with the appropriate phrasal verb:
\f0\b0 \
\
You must not __________ your hopes even when tests are challenging.\
\
(A) give up\
\
(B) look after\
\
(C) turn down\
\
(D) break out\
\

\f1\b Answer: (A) give up.
\f0\b0 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf2 Explanation:
\f0\i0  "Give up" means to stop trying or surrender hope.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf2 20. What is the meaning of the idiom: "A piece of cake"?
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) A tasty dessert served at parties\
\
(B) Something that is very easy to do\
\
(C) A difficult puzzle to solve\
\
(D) Dividing food equally among friends\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B) Something that is very easy to do.
\f0\b0 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf2 Explanation:
\f0\i0  If a task is "a piece of cake", it requires minimal effort.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf2 21. Choose the feminine gender of the noun "DRAKE":
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Goose\
\
(B) Duck\
\
(C) Peahen\
\
(D) Mare\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B) Duck.
\f0\b0 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf2 Explanation:
\f0\i0  A male duck is called a 
\f2\i drake
\f0\i0 , while the female is a 
\f2\i duck
\f0\i0 .\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf2 22. Complete the sentence with the correct question tag:
\f0\b0 \
\
She sings very melodiously, __________?\
\
(A) is she\
\
(B) doesn't she\
\
(C) didn't she\
\
(D) won't she\
\

\f1\b Answer: (B) doesn't she.
\f0\b0 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf2 Explanation:
\f0\i0  For a positive statement in simple present with third-person singular ("sings"), use the negative tag 
