\f2\i \cf2 Explanation:
\f0\i0  The standard adjective phrase is 
\f2\i fond of
\f0\i0  (meaning to like or have affection for).\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf2 26. Choose the word that does NOT belong to the group (Odd one out):
\f0\b0 \
\
(A) Cheerful\
\
(B) Delighted\
\
(C) Joyful\
\
(D) Sorrowful\
