\f1\b \cf2 Read the passage below and answer Questions 31 to 35:
\f0\b0 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 The Arctic Fox is one of nature\'92s greatest survivors. Inhabiting the treeless tundra of the Arctic, this compact creature faces winter temperatures that plummet below -50\'b0C. To endure such extreme conditions, the fox is equipped with several remarkable adaptations. Its thick, multi-layered fur is the warmest of any mammal found in the Arctic, and even the soles of its paws are heavily carpeted with fur to prevent heat loss when walking over ice.\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li4320\fi-4320\ri4320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 In addition to physical warmth, the Arctic fox possesses an ingenious camouflage system. During the frozen winter months, its coat turns pure white, blending seamlessly against the snowy wilderness to evade predators like polar bears. However, when summer arrives and the snow melts, its fur sheds and transforms into a brown or grayish hue, matching the rocky tundra soil. Small ears and a short muzzle further minimize heat dissipation, ensuring this resilient predator thrives year-round.\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li4320\fi-4320\ri4320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

